    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "5c32f915-953a-5803-af9d-db951f25ae58",
      ":question/problem": "At which point on the curve $8 x y + 4 y^{2}=- 4 x^{2} + 4 y - 4$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $j$?",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "07ebc9ba-b6a8-5b41-9175-158707557b58",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "79c6d79d-7bcd-5dd4-a961-eb7d73591705",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$(-1,1)$ only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "da5441c2-5414-5fba-a917-67d58eab9b7c",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$(1,-1)$ only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "868d784d-c944-5eab-8aee-2cbbdaf54585",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$(-1,-1)$ only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "faad3e8f-6775-5ef3-a1de-b53aa2ec1958",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$(-4,4)$ only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "d68ad81e-1f26-5ed8-a1fc-3910e4c7beaf",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$(-1,0)$ only"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "79c6d79d-7bcd-5dd4-a961-eb7d73591705"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}8 x y + 4 y^{2}&=- 4 x^{2} + 4 y - 4\\\\4 x^{2} + 8 x y + 4 y^{2} - 4 y + 4&=0\\end{aligned}$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)=4 x^{2} + 8 x y + 4 y^{2} - 4 y + 4$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$\n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$t(x,y)=f_y(x,y)\\,i-f_x(x,y)\\,j$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)&=\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(4 x^{2} + 8 x y + 4 y^{2} - 4 y + 4)\\,i-\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(4 x^{2} + 8 x y + 4 y^{2} - 4 y + 4)\\,j\\\\&=(8 x + 8 y - 4)\\,i-(8 x + 8 y)\\,j\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $j$, we must have $t\\cdot j=0.$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot j&=0\\\\- 8 x - 8 y&=0\\\\y&=-x\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSubstituting $y=-x$ into the equation of our curve gives:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}4(x+(-x))^{2}-4(-x)-(-4)&=0\\\\4x-(-4)&=0\\\\4x&=-4\\\\x&=-1\\end{aligned}$$\n\nFinally, the corresponding point is $(-1,1)$."
    },
